<title>USA: Nuclear Metals sets two-for-one stk split.</title>
<headline>Nuclear Metals sets two-for-one stk split.</headline>
<dateline>CONCORD, Mass 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nuclear Metals Inc said Thursday it will declare and pay a 100-percent stock dividend to accomplish a two-for-one stock split.  </p>
<p>The company said its proposal had yet to be approved by its shareholders.</p>
<p>It said it would pay the dividend to shareholders of record as of March 3.</p>
<p>The company, whose annual shareholders meeting it scheduled for March 26, had about 2.4 million average shares in circulation at the end of last year.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
